    <text>
        <body>
            <!-- marginal glosses on the left side of the manuscript page -->
            <ab>
                <metamark>Ø</metamark>
                <note target="#seg_Ø_1" type="commentary">
                    <p> In hac ode uelut <choice>
                            <abbr>ꝓ</abbr>
                            <expan>pro</expan>
                        </choice> sitio <choice>
                            <abbr>ẽ</abbr>
                            <expan>est</expan>
                        </choice> cuiusdam incerti carminis. nam dubitat <choice>
                            <abbr>ꝗd</abbr>
                            <expan>quid</expan>
                        </choice> primum <choice>
                            <abbr>ꝗd</abbr>
                            <expan>quid</expan>
                        </choice> potissimum dicat. utrum caelestium deorum an romanorum deorum
                        &amp; fortium ducum. omnis tamen laudat cum se fingit ancipitem.
                        peroratoriam paralexin. verum meliori intentum iam Augusti laudem extendit. <choice>
                            <abbr>ꝙ</abbr>
                            <expan>quod</expan>
                        </choice> secundum Iovem vult esse interris. Ordo <choice>
                            <abbr>÷</abbr>
                            <expan>est</expan>
                        </choice> o Clio quem virum aut quem heroam sumis celebrare tibia aut
                        acrilira </p>
                </note>
                <metamark>y</metamark>
                <note target="seg_y_1" type="commentary">
                    <p>
                        <choice>
                            <abbr>ꝓximã</abbr>
                            <expan>proximam</expan>
                        </choice> Iovis honori Minervam, <choice>
                            <abbr>ħ</abbr>
                            <expan>hoc</expan>
                        </choice>
                        <choice>
                            <abbr>ẽ</abbr>
                            <expan>est</expan>
                        </choice> virtutem et sapientiam deo uicinam, unde nulla quaestio <choice>
                            <abbr>÷</abbr>
                            <expan>est</expan>
                        </choice>. cum supra dixerit nil Iovis simile et secundum et in sequenti
                        Minervam posuit. </p>
                </note>
                <metamark>∵</metamark>
                <note target="seg_∵_1" type="commentary">
                    <p> Castorem et Pollucem Ledae filios. amatorem equorum Castorem dicit ut <choice>
                            <abbr>÷</abbr>
                            <expan>est</expan>
                        </choice> talis <choice>
                            <abbr>amrclei</abbr>
                            <expan>amoris</expan>
                        </choice> domitus Pollucis habens. Pollucem vero pugnis non bellis valentem
                        ab eo quod pugil fuerit. ergo pugnos dicit ut tertium inveniatur in genere.
                    </p>
                </note>
            </ab>

            <!-- last four lines of previous ode (carmen 1,11) with interlinear glosses -->
            <ab>
                <l> Quȩ nunc oppositis debilitat pumicibus mare </l>
                <note target="#liques_1" type="synonym">bibes</note>
                <l> Tyrrenum sapias vina <seg xml:id="liques_1">liques</seg> &amp; spatio breui </l>
                <note type="addition">l</note>
                <!-- target of gloss is unclear -->
                <note target="#reseces_1" type="synonym">auferes</note>
                <l> Spẽ longam <seg xml:id="reseces_1">reseces</seg> dum loquimur fugit inuida </l>
                <note target="Aetas_carpe_diem_quam_minimum_credula_postero_1" type="addition"> s.
                    fruere praesenti die nihil credere postero </note>
                <l>
                    <seg xml:id="Aetas_carpe_diem_quam_minimum_credula_postero_1"> Aetas. carpe
                        diem. <choice>
                            <abbr>quã</abbr>
                            <expan>quam</expan>
                        </choice>
                        <choice>
                            <abbr>minimũ</abbr>
                            <expan>minimum</expan>
                        </choice> credula postero. </seg>
                </l>
            </ab>

            <!-- beginning of current ode (carmen 1,12) -->
            <fw><hi>DE LAUDIBUS DEOꝵ UEL HOMINUM.</hi></fw>
            <!-- main text of ode including interlinear glosses -->
            <ab>
                <l>
                    <metamark><seg xml:id="seg_Ø_1">Ø</seg></metamark> Quem virum aut heroam lyra
                    vel acri </l>
                <note target="#seg_sumis_1" type="addition">contendis</note>
                <note target="#seg_clyo_1" type="explanation">una ex novem musis</note>
                <l> Tibia <seg xml:id="seg_sumis_1">sumis</seg> celebrare <seg xml:id="seg_clyo_1"
                        >Clio</seg>: </l>
                <note>sumis celebrare</note>
                <l> Quem deum, cuius retinet iocosa nomen imago </l>
                <note target="#seg_heliconis_oris_1" type="explanation"> in Parnaso monte musis
                    consecrato </note>
                <l> Aut in umbrosis <seg xml:id="seg_heliconis_oris_1">Heliconis oris</seg>. </l>
                <note target="#seg_aut_super_pindo_1" type="explanation"> mons Thraciae in quo
                    Orpheus cecinit </note>
                <l>
                    <seg xml:id="seg_aut_super_pindo_1">Aut super Pindo</seg>. <seg
                        xml:id="seg_gelidoue_in_hȩmo_1">gelidoque in Haemo</seg>. </l>
                <note target="#seg_gelidoue_in_hȩmo_1" type="explanation"> mons Thessaliae Haemus </note>
                <note target="#seg_Unde_uocalẽ_temere_in_secutę_Orphea_siluȩ_1"
                    type="explanation"> vocales omnes sumptae voces dicuntur </note>
                <l>
                    <seg xml:id="seg_Unde_uocalẽ_temere_in_secutę_Orphea_siluȩ_1"> Unde vocalem
                        temere insequutae Orphea silvae. </seg>
                </l>
                <note target="#seg_Arte_materna_1" type="explanation"> musica scilicet nam filius
                    Calliope dicitur </note>
                <l>
                    <seg xml:id="seg_Arte_materna_1">Arte materna</seg> rapidos morantes </l>
                <note target="#seg_lapsus_1" type="synonym">cursus</note>
                <l> Fluminum <seg xml:id="seg_lapsus_1">lapsus</seg> celerisque ventos </l>
                <note target="#seg_Blandũ_1" type="addition">propter</note>
                <note target="#seg_auritas_1" type="explanation">sensum audiendi habentes</note>
                <note target="#seg_ducere_1" type="addition">oblectare</note>
                <l>
                    <seg xml:id="seg_Blandũ_1">Blandum</seg> et <seg xml:id="seg_auritas_1"
                        >auritas</seg> fidibus canoris <seg xml:id="seg_ducere_1">ducere</seg>
                    quercus. </l>
                <l> Quid prius dicam solitis parentum </l>
                <l> Laudibus qui res hominum ac deorum </l>
                <note target="#seg_temperat_1" type="addition"> distinguit dimensio </note>
                <l> Qui mare et terras variisque <seg xml:id="seg_temperat_1">temperat</seg> horis </l>
                <note target="#seg_Unde_nil_maius_generatur_ipso_1" type="addition"> aquae ex illo
                    qui cuncta temperat, unde genus ducis quasi dicit Iovem super omnia sine
                    comparatione </note>
                <l>
                    <seg xml:id="seg_Unde_nil_maius_generatur_ipso_1"> Unde nihil maius generatur
                        ipso. </seg>
                </l>
                <note target="#seg_simile_1" type="addition">illi</note>
                <l> Nec ulla quicquam <seg xml:id="seg_simile_1">simile</seg> aut secundum. </l>
                <seg xml:id="seg_y_1">y</seg>
                <note target="#seg_Pallas_1" type="explanation">sapientia</note>
                <l> Proximos illi tamen occupavit <seg xml:id="seg_Pallas_1">Pallas</seg> honores. </l>
                <l> Proeliis audax neque te silebo </l>
                <note target="#seg_Liber_1" type="synonym">Bacche</note>
                <note target="#seg_seuis_inimica_uirgo_1" type="explanation"> Dianam dicit studiosa
                    venandi </note>
                <l>
                    <seg xml:id="seg_Liber_1">Liber</seg> et <seg xml:id="seg_seuis_inimica_uirgo_1"
                        > saevae inimica virgo </seg>
                </l>
                <note target="#seg_nec_te_1">scilicet silebo</note>
                <note target="#seg_certa_1" type="synonym">inevitabili</note>
                <note>o</note>
                <note target="#seg_Phoebe_1" type="explanation">Apollinem dicit</note>
                <l> Beluis nec te metuende certa <seg xml:id="seg_Phoebe_1"> Phoebe</seg> sagitta. </l>
                <note target="#seg_alciden_1" type="explanation">Herculem</note>
                <l>
                    <metamark><seg xml:id="seg_tricolon_1">∵</seg></metamark> Dicam et <seg
                        xml:id="seg_alciden_1">Alciden</seg>, <seg xml:id="seg_pueros_q̨_ledȩ_1"
                        >puerosque Ledae</seg>. </l>
                <note target="#seg_pueros_q̨_ledȩ_1" type="explanation">Castorem Pollucem</note>
                <l> Hunc equis illum superare pugnis </l>
            </ab>
            <!-- new page of manuscript (folio 8r), main text of ode resumes here with interlinear glosses -->
            <pb n="8r"/>
            <ab>
                <l>
                    <choice>
                        <abbr>Nobilẽ</abbr>
                        <expan>nobilem</expan>
                    </choice> quorum simul alba nautis Stella refulsit. </l>
                <l>Defluit saxis agitatus humor.</l>
                <l>Concidunt venti, fugiunt <choice>
                        <abbr>q;</abbr>
                        <expan>que</expan>
                    </choice> nubes.</l>
                <l> Et minax quia sic voluere ponto unda <choice>
                        <abbr>recũbit</abbr>
                        <expan>recumbit</expan>
                    </choice>
                </l>
                <seg xml:id="seg_S_1">S</seg>
                <l>
                    <seg xml:id="Romulus_post">Romulum post</seg> hos prius an quietum </l>
                <l> Pompilii regnum memor et superbos </l>
                <seg xml:id="seg_trikolon_2">∵</seg>
                <note target="#seg_Romulus_post_1" type="addition">dubito</note>
                <seg xml:id="seg_pro_1">
                    <choice>
                        <abbr>ꝓ</abbr>
                        <expan>pro</expan>
                    </choice>
                </seg>
                <l> Tarquinii fasces an Catonis nobile letum. </l>
                <seg xml:id="seg_S_2">S</seg>
                <l> Regulum et Scauros animaeque magnae </l>
                <seg xml:id="seg_SS_1">SS</seg>
                <l>
                    <choice>
                        <abbr>ꝓdigum</abbr>
                        <expan>prodigum</expan>
                    </choice> paulum superante Poeno </l>
                <seg xml:id="seg_SSS_1">SSS</seg>
                <l> Gratus insigni referam camena Fabriciumque </l>
                <seg xml:id="seg_c_1">c</seg>
                <l> Nunc et incomptis Curium capillis </l>
                <seg xml:id="seg_u_1">u</seg>
                <l> Utilem bello tulit et Camillum </l>
                <l> Saeva paupertas et avitus apto cum lare fundus. </l>
                <l> Crescit occulto velut arbor aevo </l>
                <seg xml:id="seg_Ø_2">Ø</seg>
                <l> Fama Marcelli micat inter omnis </l>
                <note type="addition">l</note>
                <l> Iulium sidus velut inter ignes luna minores </l>
                <l> Gentis humanae pater atque custos </l>
                <l> Orte Saturno tibi cura magni </l>
                <l> Caesaris fatis data, tu secundo Caesare regnes </l>
                <l> Ille seu Parthos Latio imminentes </l>
                <note target="#Egerit_1" type="synonym">subegerit</note>
                <l>
                    <seg xml:id="seg_Egerit_1">Egerit</seg> iusto domitos triumpho </l>
                <l> Siue subiectos orientis orae Seras et Indos. </l>
                <note target="#aequus_1" type="synonym">iustus</note>
                <l> Te minor Latium regit <seg xml:id="seg_aequus_1">aequus</seg> orbem. Tu gravi
                    curru quaties Olympum. </l>
                <l> Tu parvum castis inimica mittes fulmina lucis. </l>
            </ab>
            <!-- end of ode 1,12-->
            <!-- marginal glosses on the right side of the manuscript page -->
            <ab>
                <metamark>S</metamark>
                <note target="#seg_S_1" type="commentary">
                    <p> adhuc Romanos duces et nobiles <choice>
                            <abbr>p̃t̃eundo</abbr>
                            <expan>praetereundo</expan>
                        </choice> commemorat, ut Augustum praeferat cunctis. nam Romulus urbis Romae
                        conditor est. Numa Pompilius a Curibus Sabinus ad regnum vocatus sacrorum
                        inventor est. </p>
                </note>
                <metamark><hi>∵</hi></metamark>
                <note target="#seg_trikolon_2" type="commentary">
                    <p> Tarquinius quoque rex virtute magnus est; hic persecutionem posuit non
                        superbum. nam superbos fasces nobiles dicit. </p>
                </note>
                <metamark><hi>
                        <choice>
                            <abbr>ꝓ</abbr>
                            <expan>pro</expan>
                        </choice>
                    </hi></metamark>
                <note target="#seg_ꝓ_1" type="commentary">
                    <p> Cato dum mortuo Pompeio apud Uticam obsideret, amore libertatis manu sua se
                        ipsum peremit. unde et Uticensis vocatus est. </p>
                </note>
                <metamark><hi>S</hi></metamark>
                <note target="#seg_S_2" type="commentary">
                    <p> Regulum autem cum Afris vicisset ab hisdem cum paucis captus est. quem dum
                        Carthaginienses Romae misissent pro commutatione captivorum, adquiescentes
                        Romanos suo consilio revocavit. hunc Poeni dum memoria sacramenti violaret,
                        sectis palpebris vigiliis necaverunt. </p>
                </note>
                <metamark><hi>SS</hi></metamark>
                <note target="#seg_SS_1" type="commentary">
                    <p> Paulus et Terentius Varro consules adversus Hannibalem missi sunt. hi
                        similiter apud Cannas Apuliae vicum grandi exercitu Romani clade superati
                        sunt. Paulus postea quam tantam vitio collegae sui vidisset stragem, se
                        inimicis dedit. </p>
                </note>
                <metamark><hi>SSS</hi></metamark>
                <note target="#seg_SSS_1" type="commentary">
                    <p> Fabricius quoque magnis primus a rege Pyrrho tentatus, dum nimis pauper
                        censu esset, corrumpi non potuit. de quo Lucanus: quod te Fabricius regi non
                        vendidit auro. </p>
                </note>
                <metamark><hi>c</hi></metamark>
                <note target="#seg_c_1" type="commentary">
                    <p> Curius paupertate clarus, de agro ad consulatum evocatus est, qui non
                        totondit caesariem propter iniuriam capturam. </p>
                </note>
                <metamark><hi>u</hi></metamark>
                <note target="#seg_u_1" type="commentary">
                    <p> Camillus de exilio reversus victores Gallos urbe pepulit, et ad
                        internitionem cecidit. victor quo sua sponte in exilium rediit. </p>
                </note>
            </ab>


            <ab>
                <metamark>Ø</metamark>
                <note target="#seg_Ø_2" type="commentary">
                    <p> Marcellus Octaviae dicitur filius sororis Caesaris, qui puer mortuus est. de
                        quo Virgilius: si qua fata aspera rumpas tu Marcellus eris. Aut illum
                        commemorat qui primus Hannibalem apud Nolam civitatem in fugam compulit et
                        ab eo postea occisus est. </p>
                </note>
            </ab>
        </body>
    </text>
</TEI>
